## 6. How CVSS severity translates to dollars

| CVSS severity | In KEV? | Scenarios | Average standalone ALE | Sum of standalone ALE |
|---|:---:|---:|---:|---:|
{% for row in r.severity %}
| {{ row.severity }} | {{ "yes" if row.kev_flag else "no" }} | {{ row.scenarios }} | {{ row.avg_ale|money }} | {{ row.total_ale|money }} |
{% endfor %}

CVSS measures *theoretical* severity. KEV membership is evidence of *actual* exploitation, and in this
model it multiplies exploit probability by {{ r.assumptions.kev_multiplier|num(0) }}×. That is why a HIGH CVE that is actively
exploited can outrank a CRITICAL one that is not.

